Description: Privacy-first, zero-telemetry Telegram Desktop client
 TruthGram is a GPL-3.0 fork of telegramdesktop/tdesktop that adds a curated
 set of privacy, UX, and power-user modules without any third-party analytics,
 tracking, or proprietary blobs. All sync state travels through the user's own
 Telegram Saved Messages, encrypted with AES-256-GCM keyed off the MTProto
 auth key.
 .
 Built-in modules include an iOS-inspired frosted-glass UI, a detachable FFT
 mini media player, a voice changer hooking tg_owt pre-Opus, Ghost Mode read/
 unread controls, screenshot capture protection, a Mini App domain inspector,
 a local Sherlock-style OSINT runner over Tor/SOCKS5, a link phishing
 analyzer, a visual BotFather builder, P2P chess, and a Termux/local CLI IPC
 bridge. A sandboxed plugin engine supports native .so and Lua scripts.
